<!-- VIP — the subscription's own destination, the centre tab in the category's bar. Built
     to the reference: a gold masthead, the wallet card, two merchandising rails, the
     benefit list — then the tiers themselves.

     FUNNEL ROLE: justify the subscription price. Which is exactly why every claim here is
     the DATA'S claim: the rails are named for what they bind ("Watch free with VIP" is
     true of the whole catalogue; "Recently added" is the latest rail) — a "VIP-only"
     shelf of ordinary trending shows is a lie on the one screen whose job is trust.
     Entitlement is read from /wallet/state (`vip`), never assumed, and every price comes
     from /store/catalog so an operator changes it without a build. Buying routes to the
     one checkout path in /store.

     THE SAME RULE APPLIES TO THE BENEFIT LIST, and for a while it did not. This card sold
     "1080p", "Offline downloads" and "No ads" against a build that could render none of
     them — the first two are impossible here and are now deleted, the third is now
     implemented in <AdGate>. The list below is derived from what `server/*.dsx` grants and
     nothing else; every row names the action that makes it true. A benefit list on a paid
     screen is a contract, and this file is the reference thousands of apps will copy. -->

<vstack class="screen" style:web="min-height: {{ dsx.screen.height }}px">
  <head>
    <expects variable="nav"/>

    <api as="session" url="/dev-session.json" ssr="false"/>
    <api as="wallet" url="/wallet/state" ssr="false" needs="session" headers="dsx.variable.authHeaders" on:success="global.cacheWallet = wallet.data"/>
    <api as="catalog" url="/store/catalog" on:success="global.cacheCatalog = catalog.data"/>
    <api as="home" url="/catalog/home" on:success="global.cacheHome = home.data"/>

    <variable as="hovId">return ''</variable>
    <!-- ══ THE BENEFIT LIST IS A CONTRACT, AND IT IS READ OFF THE SERVER ═══════════════
         This list used to sell four things. Two of them did not exist:

         · "1080p high quality" — DELETED, not deferred. `<video>` has no quality attribute
           on any renderer (upstream #270 / PLAN.md §36), so there is no rendition to sell.
           This template already made this exact call once: Phase 1 deleted the 240p–1080p
           ladder from the player's options sheet, and the comment it left behind
           (Components/Watch.dsx:1172-1175) says why — "it priced 1080p behind VIP, which
           made it a paywall on a no-op". Selling it here was the same paywall, re-erected
           one screen away from where it was removed. The player still names the gap where
           quality lives ("Adaptive — one rendition in this build"); a purchase screen is
           not the place to re-advertise it, because a "coming soon" beside a price is still
           a reason to pay today for something undated.
         · "Offline downloads" — DELETED. Nothing in this app downloads anything: no file
           plane, no offline store, no queue, no settings. The player's Download rail control
           routed to /vip, so the feature's only implementation was a link to the screen
           selling it — that control has since been deleted too, along with the drawer's
           second copy of it. Inventing a fake download would have been worse than either.

         What remains is what `server/*.dsx` actually grants, and each row can be checked:

           unlocked   `unlockEpisode` prices at 0 when the wallet's `vip_until` is in the
                      future — server/wallet.dsx:190-192. It has no catalogue exceptions, so
                      it covers shows added after the pass was bought.
           coins      because that price is 0, the spend path never runs: no ledger row, no
                      wallet debit (server/wallet.dsx:194-210). The balance survives the pass.
           no ads     TRUE AS OF THIS PASS, not before. <AdGate> now takes `vip=` and refuses
                      in its own action (Components/parts/AdGate.dsx), and Rewards.dsx passes
                      the entitlement. Implementing it was cheaper than deleting it, and it
                      is the benefit a member actually notices.

         THREE ROWS, NOT FOUR. The list is shorter than the design that preceded it because
         the backend grants two things and the client adds one. Padding it back to four would
         re-create the defect this pass removed. -->
    <variable as="benefits">
      return [
        { id: 'b1', icon: 'lock.open.fill',        label: 'Every episode unlocked', note: 'Paid episodes open at 0 coins, on every series in the catalogue — including the ones added while your pass runs' },
        { id: 'b2', icon: 'dollarsign.circle.fill', label: 'Your coins stay yours',  note: 'A VIP unlock debits nothing, so the balance you bought is still there when the pass ends' },
        { id: 'b3', icon: 'bolt.fill',             label: 'No ads',                 note: 'The one rewarded ad this app shows is switched off while your pass is active' }
      ]
    </variable>
    <!-- stale-then-fresh: the api cache dies with the mount (PLAN.md §6.30), so the
         last good payload lives in the app-wide store and is the FIRST PAINT while the
         refetch runs. Read homeView, never home.data, or the blank frame returns. -->
    <!-- stale-then-fresh: the api cache dies with the mount (PLAN.md §6.30), so the
         last good payload lives in the app-wide store and is the FIRST PAINT while the
         refetch runs. Read catalogView, never catalog.data, or the blank frame returns. -->
    <!-- stale-then-fresh: the api cache dies with the mount (PLAN.md §6.30), so the
         last good payload lives in the app-wide store and is the FIRST PAINT while the
         refetch runs. Read walletView, never wallet.data, or the blank frame returns. -->
    <variable as="walletView" computed="true">
      if (wallet.data != null) { return wallet.data }
      return global.cacheWallet
    </variable>
    <variable as="catalogView" computed="true">
      if (catalog.data != null) { return catalog.data }
      return global.cacheCatalog
    </variable>
    <variable as="homeView" computed="true">
      if (home.data != null) { return home.data }
      return global.cacheHome
    </variable>
    <variable as="authHeaders" computed="true">
      if (session.data == null) { return {} }
      return { authorization: 'Bearer ' + session.data.viewer.token }
    </variable>
    <variable as="bp" computed="true">
      const w = dsx.screen.width
      if (w >= 1120) { return 'desktop' }
      if (w >= 768) { return 'tablet' }
      return 'phone'
    </variable>
    <variable as="wide" computed="true">return dsx.variable.bp != 'phone'</variable>
    <variable as="gutter" computed="true">
      if (dsx.variable.bp == 'desktop') { return 86 }
      if (dsx.variable.bp == 'tablet') { return 40 }
      return 16
    </variable>
    <variable as="shell" computed="true">
      const g = dsx.variable.gutter
      return 'width: 100%; max-width: 1100px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding-left: ' + g + 'px; padding-right: ' + g + 'px'
    </variable>
    <!-- a rail track is `max-content` with the gutter as its padding: `width: 100%` (the
         page-shell recipe) caps the track at the scroller and the cards eat the difference. -->
    <variable as="railShell" computed="true">
      const g = dsx.variable.gutter
      const over = dsx.screen.width - 1440
      const lead = g + (over > 0 ? Math.round(over / 2) : 0)
      return 'width: max-content; padding-left: ' + lead + 'px; padding-right: ' + lead + 'px'
    </variable>
    <variable as="mastheadBox" computed="true">
      return dsx.variable.shell + '; background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(246,182,61,0.16) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0) 100%)'
    </variable>
    <variable as="isVip" computed="true">
      if (dsx.variable.walletView == null) { return false }
      return dsx.variable.walletView.vip === true
    </variable>
    <!-- THE SERVER GRANTS A DATED PASS AND THIS SCREEN NEVER SAID SO. `walletState` returns
         `vipUntil` (server/wallet.dsx:46) and the only thing read here was the boolean —
         so a member could not find out when their access ended on the screen that sold it.
         Same ISO slice as Components/Profile.dsx:61-64, which is this app's one date idiom
         until real formatting lands (G18). -->
    <variable as="vipUntil" computed="true">
      if (dsx.variable.walletView == null || dsx.variable.walletView.vipUntil == null) { return '' }
      return String(dsx.variable.walletView.vipUntil).slice(0, 10)
    </variable>
    <variable as="statusLine" computed="true">
      if (dsx.variable.vipUntil == '') { return 'VIP active' }
      return 'VIP active through ' + dsx.variable.vipUntil
    </variable>
    <!-- WHAT A PLAN ACTUALLY IS ON THIS BACKEND, derived from the same table the tiers are
         priced from rather than typed in here. `createCheckout` opens a ONE-OFF Stripe
         PaymentIntent (server/store.dsx:88-95) and `settleOrder` stamps
         `vip_until = now + days` (server/store.dsx:150-151). There is no Stripe Subscription
         object, no renewal, no cancel path — so a pass runs its term and stops.

         THIS CONTRADICTS THE TIER CARDS BELOW, ON PURPOSE. `storeCatalog` ships
         `note: 'Auto-renew. Cancel anytime.'` on two tiers and 'then $14.99/week' on the
         third (server/store.dsx:34-36), and <PlansSheet> renders those strings verbatim.
         Those notes are false and they live in a document this pass does not own; the fix
         is filed as a handoff. Until it lands, the screen whose stated job is trust states
         what the build does rather than repeating a claim it cannot back — the contradiction
         being visible is the point of a loud bridge (Article 7). -->
    <variable as="termLine" computed="true">
      const c = dsx.variable.catalogView
      const tail = ' When the date passes VIP simply stops — your coins are not affected.'
      if (c == null || c.vip == null || c.vip.length == 0) {
        return 'Every plan is a one-time charge for a pass that runs a fixed number of days.' + tail
      }
      let days = ''
      for (const t of c.vip) { days = days == '' ? String(t.days) : days + ', ' + String(t.days) }
      return 'Every plan is a one-time charge for a dated pass — ' + days + ' days. This build has no auto-renewal.' + tail
    </variable>
    <!-- RESTORE, honestly. Apple requires "a way for current subscribers to sign in or
         restore purchases" on a subscription sign-up screen. Entitlement here is not a
         StoreKit receipt — it is a column on the caller's wallet row, so the real restore is
         "re-read this account", which is exactly what this does and all it can do. The half
         that is missing is the OTHER half of Apple's sentence: there is no sign-in anywhere
         in this app (the session is a static JSON file — docs/auth.md), so a member on a new
         device cannot reach their account to restore onto it. The row says both. -->
    <variable as="restoreLine" computed="true">
      if (wallet.loading) { return 'Checking this account…' }
      if (dsx.variable.walletView == null) { return 'Could not read this account. Try again.' }
      if (dsx.variable.isVip) { return 'Found: ' + dsx.variable.statusLine + '.' }
      return 'No active pass on this account.'
    </variable>
    <variable as="posterW" computed="true">return dsx.variable.bp == 'phone' ? 150 : 186</variable>
    <variable as="phase" computed="true">
      if (catalog.error != null || home.error != null) { return 'error' }
      if (dsx.variable.catalogView == null || dsx.variable.homeView == null) { return 'loading' }
      return 'content'
    </variable>

    <formula as="railFx" id="item.id">
      const on = dsx.variable.hovId == id
      return 'width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3/4; border-radius: 10px; object-fit: cover; transition: transform 0.22s ease; transform: scale(' + (on ? 1.03 : 1) + ')'
    </formula>

    <style as="screen" background="#000000" alignItems="stretch" grow="true" spacing="0"/>
    <style as="scroller" alignItems="stretch"/>
    <style as="page" spacing="0" paddingBottom="34" alignItems="stretch"/>
    <style as="masthead" alignItems="center" spacing="8" paddingTop="20" paddingBottom="22"/>
    <style as="mastheadTitle" fontSize="20" fontWeight="bold" color="#F6B63D" textAlign="center"/>
    <style as="section" spacing="14" alignItems="stretch" paddingTop="28"/>
    <style as="sectionTitle" fontSize="20" fontWeight="bold" color="#F6B63D" textAlign="center"/>
    <style as="rowTitle" fontSize="17" fontWeight="bold" color="#FFFFFF"/>

    <style as="watchCard" background="#1A1A1C" radius="14" paddingH="18" paddingV="16" alignItems="center" spacing="12"/>
    <style as="watchCap" fontSize="14" color="rgba(255,255,255,0.55)"/>
    <style as="watchNum" fontSize="24" fontWeight="bold" color="#F6B63D"/>
    <style as="watchLink" fontSize="14" color="#F6B63D"/>

    <style as="rail" spacing="12" alignItems="flex-start"/>
    <style as="card" spacing="8" alignItems="stretch"/>
    <style as="cardTitle" fontSize="14" color="rgba(255,255,255,0.9)" lineLimit="2" lineSpacing="2"/>
    <style as="vipTag" background="#F6B63D" radius="4" paddingH="7" paddingV="2" fontSize="11" fontWeight="bold" color="#3A2A08"/>
    <style as="tagWrap" paddingTrailing="8" paddingTop="8" alignItems="flex-end" zIndex="1"/>
    <style as="dateRow" spacing="9" alignItems="center" paddingBottom="4"/>
    <style as="dateTxt" fontSize="13" color="rgba(255,255,255,0.55)"/>

    <style as="benefitRow" spacing="14" alignItems="center" paddingV="14"/>
    <style as="benefitLabel" fontSize="16" color="#FFFFFF"/>
    <style as="benefitNote" fontSize="13" color="rgba(255,255,255,0.45)" lineSpacing="3"/>
    <!-- the disclosure rows: same rhythm as a benefit row, deliberately not the same voice —
         no gold icon, no white headline unless the row is itself a control -->
    <style as="discRow" spacing="14" alignItems="flex-start" paddingV="12"/>
    <style as="restoreBtn" background="#26262C" radius="18" paddingH="16" paddingV="12" fontSize="13" fontWeight="semibold" color="#FFFFFF"/>

    <style as="tierCard" radius="14" paddingH="18" paddingV="18" spacing="8" alignItems="flex-start"/>
    <style as="tierName" fontSize="15" fontWeight="semibold" color="#3A2A08"/>
    <style as="tierPrice" fontSize="24" fontWeight="bold" color="#2A1D04"/>
    <style as="tierNote" fontSize="12" color="rgba(42,29,4,0.7)"/>
    <style as="tierBadge" background="#FF2C55" radius="4" paddingH="7" paddingV="3" fontSize="11" fontWeight="bold" color="#FFFFFF"/>
    <style as="cta" background="#FF2C55" radius="24" paddingV="15" fontSize="16" fontWeight="semibold" color="#FFFFFF"/>
    <style as="statusPill" background="rgba(246,182,61,0.16)" radius="14" paddingH="14" paddingV="8" spacing="7" alignItems="center"/>
    <style as="statusTxt" fontSize="13" fontWeight="semibold" color="#F6B63D"/>
    <style as="skeleton" background="#141419" radius="14"/>
    <style as="errCard" background="#141419" radius="14" spacing="10" paddingH="16" paddingV="20" alignItems="center"/>
    <style as="retryBtn" background="#FF2C55" radius="20" paddingH="20" paddingV="12" fontSize="14" fontWeight="semibold" color="#FFFFFF"/>
  </head>

  <scroll class="scroller" style="flex: 1; min-height: 0">
    <vstack class="page">
      <TopNav active="vip" visible-if="dsx.variable.wide"/>

      <vstack class="masthead" style="{{ dsx.variable.mastheadBox }}">
        <image src="/assets/coin.svg" a11yHidden="true" style="width: 54px; height: 54px"/>
        <text value="Enjoy Your VIP Access and Privileges" class="mastheadTitle"/>
        <hstack class="statusPill" visible-if="dsx.variable.isVip">
          <image icon="crown.fill" iconSize="13" color="#F6B63D" a11yHidden="true"/>
          <text value="{{ dsx.variable.statusLine }}" class="statusTxt"/>
        </hstack>
      </vstack>

      <vstack style="{{ dsx.variable.shell }}" alignItems="stretch">
        <hstack class="watchCard">
          <vstack spacing="4" style="flex: 1">
            <text value="Your wallet" class="watchCap"/>
            <hstack spacing="6" alignItems="flex-end">
              <text value="{{ dsx.variable.walletView == null ? '—' : dsx.variable.walletView.coins + dsx.variable.walletView.bonus }}" class="watchNum"/>
              <text value="coins" class="watchCap" style="padding-bottom: 4px"/>
            </hstack>
          </vstack>
          <hstack spacing="4" alignItems="center" on:tap="dsx.module.route.reset({ path: '/profile' })"
                  a11yGroup="true" a11yTrait="button" a11yLabel="View your wallet">
            <text value="View wallet" class="watchLink"/>
            <image icon="chevron.right" iconSize="12" color="#F6B63D" a11yHidden="true"/>
          </hstack>
        </hstack>
      </vstack>

      <vstack class="section" visible-if="dsx.variable.phase == 'loading'">
        <vstack style="{{ dsx.variable.shell }}" spacing="14" alignItems="stretch">
          <Skeleton height="200" radius="14"/>
          <Skeleton height="120" radius="14"/>
        </vstack>
      </vstack>
      <vstack class="section" visible-if="dsx.variable.phase == 'error'">
        <vstack style="{{ dsx.variable.shell }}" alignItems="stretch">
          <vstack class="errCard">
            <text value="VIP plans could not be loaded." fontSize="14" color="#FFFFFF"/>
            <button label="Retry" class="retryBtn" on:tap="catalog.refresh()"/>
          </vstack>
        </vstack>
      </vstack>

      <!-- what VIP unlocks, shown on the shows people are actually watching: every one of
           these has locked episodes a member never pays for -->
      <vstack class="section" visible-if="dsx.variable.phase == 'content'">
        <text value="Watch free with VIP" class="sectionTitle"/>
        <scroll axis="horizontal" indicators="false">
          <hstack class="rail" style="{{ dsx.variable.railShell }}">
            <list bind="dsx.variable.homeView.trending" key="id" axis="horizontal" scroll="false" spacing="12">
              <vstack class="card" style="width: {{ dsx.variable.posterW }}px" href="/watch/{{ item.id }}/1"
                      on:hoverStart="dsx.variable.hovId = item.id" on:hoverEnd="dsx.variable.hovId = ''"
                      a11yGroup="true" a11yLabel="{{ item.title }}">
                <zstack>
                  <image src="{{ item.poster }}" contentFit="cover" a11yHidden="true" style="{{ railFx }}"/>
                  <vstack class="tagWrap" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none">
                    <text value="VIP" class="vipTag"/>
                  </vstack>
                </zstack>
                <text value="{{ item.title }}" class="cardTitle" style="display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 2; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; overflow: hidden"/>
              </vstack>
            </list>
          </hstack>
        </scroll>
      </vstack>

      <!-- recently added -->
      <vstack class="section" visible-if="dsx.variable.phase == 'content'">
        <text value="Recently added" class="sectionTitle"/>
        <scroll axis="horizontal" indicators="false">
          <hstack class="rail" style="{{ dsx.variable.railShell }}">
            <list bind="dsx.variable.homeView.latest" key="id" axis="horizontal" scroll="false" spacing="12">
              <vstack class="card" style="width: {{ dsx.variable.posterW }}px" href="/show/{{ item.id }}"
                      on:hoverStart="dsx.variable.hovId = item.id" on:hoverEnd="dsx.variable.hovId = ''"
                      a11yGroup="true" a11yLabel="{{ item.title }}">
                <image src="{{ item.poster }}" contentFit="cover" a11yHidden="true" style="{{ railFx }}"/>
                <text value="{{ item.title }}" class="cardTitle" style="display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 2; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; overflow: hidden"/>
              </vstack>
            </list>
          </hstack>
        </scroll>
      </vstack>

      <!-- benefits — three rows, each one a thing server/*.dsx actually does. See the
           `benefits` variable in the head for what was removed and why. -->
      <vstack class="section" visible-if="dsx.variable.phase != 'error'">
        <text value="Your Benefits" class="sectionTitle"/>
        <vstack style="{{ dsx.variable.shell }}" alignItems="stretch">
          <list bind="dsx.variable.benefits" key="id" scroll="false" spacing="0">
            <hstack class="benefitRow">
              <image icon="{{ item.icon }}" iconSize="20" color="#F6B63D" a11yHidden="true"/>
              <vstack spacing="3" style="flex: 1; min-width: 0">
                <text value="{{ item.label }}" class="benefitLabel"/>
                <text value="{{ item.note }}" class="benefitNote"/>
              </vstack>
            </hstack>
          </list>

          <!-- THE TERM. A disclosure, not a perk — so it sits under the list in the quiet
               style rather than wearing a gold icon and pretending to be a fourth benefit.
               Apple's sign-up-screen rules want the duration and what the period provides
               stated on this screen; this is the duration half. -->
          <hstack class="discRow">
            <image icon="clock.fill" iconSize="15" color="rgba(255,255,255,0.45)" a11yHidden="true"/>
            <text value="{{ dsx.variable.termLine }}" class="benefitNote" style="flex: 1; min-width: 0"/>
          </hstack>

          <!-- RESTORE PURCHASES — required on a subscription sign-up screen, and here it is
               the real (small) thing this backend supports: re-read the account's
               entitlement. The second line names the half that is missing rather than
               letting the button imply a device-to-device restore it cannot do. -->
          <hstack class="discRow">
            <image icon="arrow.clockwise" iconSize="15" color="rgba(255,255,255,0.45)" a11yHidden="true"/>
            <vstack spacing="3" style="flex: 1; min-width: 0">
              <text value="Restore purchases" class="benefitLabel"/>
              <text value="{{ dsx.variable.restoreLine }}" class="benefitNote"/>
              <text value="VIP is held on your account, not on this device, so restoring re-reads the account you are signed in to. This build has no sign-in yet, so a pass bought on another account cannot be reached from here." class="benefitNote"/>
            </vstack>
            <button label="Restore" class="restoreBtn" on:tap="wallet.refresh()"/>
          </hstack>

          <!-- TERMS AND PRIVACY — required in-app beside a subscription, and genuinely
               absent: no URL exists in App.json, dsx.json or dsx.config.json, and there is
               no legal surface anywhere in Components/. A placeholder link would be worse
               than nothing, so the row states the gap the way the player's Quality row and
               Profile's Language row state theirs (Article 7). This app cannot be submitted
               to either store until an adopter fills it in, and now that fact is visible in
               the product instead of only in an audit. -->
          <hstack class="discRow" a11yGroup="true"
                  a11yLabel="Terms of Use and Privacy Policy: this build ships no legal links. An adopter must add them before submitting to a store.">
            <image icon="lock.shield" iconSize="15" color="rgba(255,255,255,0.45)" a11yHidden="true"/>
            <text value="Terms of Use and Privacy Policy — not set in this build. Both stores require them in-app beside a paid plan; an adopter points these at their own URLs before submitting." class="benefitNote" style="flex: 1; min-width: 0"/>
          </hstack>
        </vstack>
      </vstack>

      <!-- the tiers — the SAME component the Profile card raises and the Store embeds, so
           VIP's own plan list buys through the one checkout instead of bouncing to /store -->
      <vstack class="section" visible-if="dsx.variable.phase == 'content'">
        <text value="Choose your plan" class="sectionTitle"/>
        <vstack style="{{ dsx.variable.shell }}" alignItems="stretch" spacing="12">
          <PlansSheet mode="inline" headers="{{ dsx.variable.authHeaders }}"
                      vip="{{ dsx.variable.isVip }}" on:purchased="wallet.refresh()"/>
        </vstack>
      </vstack>
    </vstack>
  </scroll>
  <TabBar active="vip" visible-if="dsx.variable.wide == false"/>
</vstack>
